  "note": "Liquid's d1-2B decision model: the LFM3-VL-2B text tower (model_type lfm3_vl) post-trained for single-pass typed answers, distinguished from the generative checkpoint by the GGUF's lfm3.decision.type=lfm3-d1 and the config's D1Model architecture. Its GGUF declares attention.causal false, which the runtime serves causally — a score-only decision model never decodes, and its calibrated readout rides the last-position logits either way. Served text-only: the vision tower's tensors install unread (no tower support). No draft: a decision model never decodes, so speculative decode weights would install unused.",
